      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. Let's get straight to the point. To avoid the SettingWithCopyWarning when adding a new column to a sliced DataFrame, you can use the `.loc` method to ensure you're modifying the original DataFrame. Here's how you can do it:\n\n```python\n# Assuming 'df' is your original DataFrame and you want to add a new column 'new_col'\n# to the sliced DataFrame 'sliced_df' which is a slice of 'df'.\n\n# First, make sure 'sliced_df' is a slice of 'df'\nsliced_df = df.loc[some_condition]  # Replace 'some_condition' with your actual condition\n\n# Now, to add a new column to the original DataFrame 'df', not the sliced one:\ndf.loc[some_condition, 'new_col'] = some_value  # Replace 'some_value' with the value you want to assign\n\n# If you want to add a new column to the sliced DataFrame, you should do it like this:\nsliced_df['new_col'] = some_value  # This will add 'new_col' to 'sliced_df' without causing a warning\n```\n\nBy using `.loc`, you're explicitly telling pandas",
      "source": "target",
